<h2 id=3D"1">k7 0.9.0: record and replay CLI outputs</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-1">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-k7-0-9-0-record-and-rep=
lay-cli-outputs/18660/1">https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-k7-0-9-0-record-an=
d-replay-cli-outputs/18660/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org1b57b63" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org1b57b63">Thomas Gazagnaire announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org1b57b63">
<p>
I'm happy to announce the release of <a href=3D"https://github.com/samoht/o=
caml-k7">k7 0.9.0</a> a small tool to record and replay CLI animations.
</p>

<p>
It's available on MacOS and Linux with <code>brew</code>:
</p>

<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"org3179159">
brew install samoht/tap/k7
</pre>

<p>
or in opam:
</p>

<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"org9592e8a">
opam install k7
</pre>

<p>
The main feature vs. other similar tools is that it can use cram tests as i=
nput or output, so you can 1/ convert any cram test into an svg file; and 2=
/ ensure the svg that you use in your README files stays up-to-date with yo=
ur code.
</p>

<p>
Apart from this it's in pure OCaml with no browser or ffmpeg involved; it p=
lays <code>.cast</code> and <code>.tape</code> files (from <code>asciinema<=
/code> and <code>vhs</code>) and write <code>.cast</code> files, but probab=
ly has fewer options than those tools, so feel free to open <a href=3D"http=
s://github.com/samoht/ocaml-k7/issues">an issue</a> if you find anything mi=
ssing or not working.
</p>

<p>
See more details in my post: <a href=3D"https://gazagnaire.org/blog/2026-10=
-26-k7.html">https://gazagnaire.org/blog/2026-10-26-k7.html</a>
</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-2" class=3D"outline-2">
<h2 id=3D"2">dune tracing</h2>
<div class=3D"outline-text-2" id=3D"text-2">
<p>
Archive: <a href=3D"https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/blog-dune-tracing/18670/1">=
https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/blog-dune-tracing/18670/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id=3D"outline-container-org47fb2e4" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org47fb2e4">Rapha=C3=ABl Proust announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org47fb2e4">
<p>
Over the summer, @NatKarmios worked on <code>dune</code> for his internship=
 at [Ahrefs](ahrefs.com).
He got <a href=3D"https://github.com/ocaml/dune/pulls?q=3Dis%3Apr+author%3A=
NatKarmios">a couple of PRs merged into dune</a>. Then he wrote a new backe=
nd for traces and a matching perfetto extension.
</p>

<p>
All of the details in his blog post:=20=20
<a href=3D"https://tech.ahrefs.com/tracing-dune-with-a-side-of-graphs-56603=
d7794bc">Tracing Dune, with a side of graphs</a>
</p>

<p>
TL;DR: you get a graph view of the build, some SQL querying capabilities, i=
t scales to handle Ahrefs' monorepo
</p>

<p>
We're using the new tracing capability internally. And we're planning on up=
streaming it too.
</p>
</div>
