<div id=3D"outline-container-org86a7bf6" class=3D"outline-3">
<h3 id=3D"org86a7bf6">Thomas Gazagnaire announced</h3>
<div class=3D"outline-text-3" id=3D"text-org86a7bf6">
<p>
I'm happy to announce the release of <a href=3D"https://github.com/samoht/o=
caml-console">console 0.9.0</a>, a set of widgets for building nice-looking=
 command-line tools. The main design constraint I tried to follow is that t=
he output should look good both for a human at an interactive terminal and =
for scripts run in CI or other non-interactive loops (like LLM agents). Liv=
e rows are redrawn in place and everything useful the program printed is st=
ill there when it ends; piped output tries to be relatively clean.
</p>


<div id=3D"org76cf378" class=3D"figure">
<p><img src=3D"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex020/uploads/ocaml/original=
/2X/2/21b202a69ab6ff219fa5fee2416d438bbae78d14.gif" alt=3D"21b202a69ab6ff21=
9fa5fee2416d438bbae78d14.gif" width=3D"80%" />
</p>
</div>

<p>
You can use it with:
</p>

<pre class=3D"example" id=3D"org066d1a3">
opam install console console-eio
</pre>

<p>
The widgets in <code>console</code> are pure; <code>console-eio</code> is t=
he driver that runs animations. There are a few limitation (including limit=
ed Windows support) but you can already use it to encode quite complex UX. =
For instance, here a few imitations of package manager frontends using cons=
ole (recorded using <a href=3D"https://gazagnaire.org/blog/2026-10-26-k7.ht=
ml">k7</a>):
</p>


<div id=3D"orgc38aba2" class=3D"figure">
<p><img src=3D"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex020/uploads/ocaml/original=
/2X/b/b18c267eea031cfb770f92fab15f9355882c96d4.gif" alt=3D"b18c267eea031cfb=
770f92fab15f9355882c96d4.gif" width=3D"80%" />
</p>
</div>


<div id=3D"orga38c1a2" class=3D"figure">
<p><img src=3D"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex020/uploads/ocaml/original=
/2X/e/ed712dd72eba5421dc825b884e0dbb739b2befdc.gif" alt=3D"ed712dd72eba5421=
dc825b884e0dbb739b2befdc.gif" width=3D"80%" />
</p>
</div>


<div id=3D"org8563c9f" class=3D"figure">
<p><img src=3D"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex020/uploads/ocaml/original=
/2X/d/d7a8c56d42c8430f282e7afa9426bb315b52965f.gif" alt=3D"d7a8c56d42c8430f=
282e7afa9426bb315b52965f.gif" width=3D"80%" />
</p>
</div>


<div id=3D"orgfbe0ba8" class=3D"figure">
<p><img src=3D"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/flex020/uploads/ocaml/original=
/2X/7/7ecc3d918f9968f61a15ef66e563487cd70335ee.gif" alt=3D"7ecc3d918f9968f6=
1a15ef66e563487cd70335ee.gif" width=3D"80%" />
</p>
</div>

<p>
You can read more (including how it compares with notty, progress and print=
box, here): <a href=3D"https://gazagnaire.org/blog/2026-11-02-console.html"=
>https://gazagnaire.org/blog/2026-11-02-console.html</a>.
</p>

<p>
Feedback is very welcome before 1.0, on the <a href=3D"https://github.com/s=
amoht/ocaml-console/issues">issue tracker</a> or here.
</p>
